From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Barnes <hello@jonbarnes.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:13:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] The light rules that worked become the rule, and the drawn beam stays

Patch 0057 of the renderer series (OoT: Recompiled).

The user, 2026-10-12, of the build carrying 0056 at its defaults: "same with the light beam
fixes" (PERFECT). Under their standing rule a confirmed fix leaves the Debugging menu, so the two
rules that were on are simply the rule: a see-through draw with a fading texture, or one added
over what is behind it, is light, casts no shadow and takes none. The gray texture and long shape
candidates, never needed, are gone, and tuneLightTest.z is unused again.

And the game's drawn shaft is always drawn. 0034 and 0039 drew a slanted shaft as nothing in a
place with windows while the local lights were traced, 0051's Drawn beam row could show it, and
it defaulted to hidden, which is how the sword room's beam went ("i want to add that beam back
in"). The hiding, the row's tuneShafts.z and RtConfig::drawnBeam are removed.

